WHAT IS THE MAINTANENCE WORK IN DOCKER?
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
All the metadata of docker [images, host, cont details etc etc] will be stored at "var/lib/docker". 
So the maintenance work is we need to make sure that the "var/lib/docker" repo has enough capacity.

Actions or tasks:
1. Ensure that all the images are having ref to ID. if the imaage is not having proper tag or repo location the we need to delete that image.
2. Ensure images are dandling i.e. images should have cache and proper ref.
3. when we create docker run, new image is downloaded. so we need to make sure the older images are deleted
4. delete exited containers
5. delete unused volumes
